<div class="section" id="recommendations">
  <h2>6. Strategic Recommendations</h2>
  <p class="section-desc">Synthesized, prioritized recommendations based on the cross-app analysis, tailored for competitive positioning, feature prioritization, and retention strategy.</p>

  <div class="rec-grid">
    <div class="rec-card" style="border-left: 4px solid #ef4444;">
      <div class="rec-priority" style="color: #ef4444;">P0 &mdash; Critical</div>
      <h4>1. Reassess Rate Limiting & Free-Tier Generosity</h4>
      <p>Claude's 8.0% pricing complaint rate and Perplexity's 7.5% are the single largest drivers of dissatisfaction. These reviews attract 3&ndash;6&times; more engagement than general reviews, amplifying the churn signal. Benchmark against Copilot's approach (2.2% rate) where generous free-tier access drives a 68% 5-star rate. Consider expanding free usage limits or introducing an intermediate tier to convert frustrated free users before they defect.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rec-card" style="border-left: 4px solid #ef4444;">
      <div class="rec-priority" style="color: #ef4444;">P0 &mdash; Critical</div>
      <h4>2. Prioritize Mobile App Stability (Bugs/Performance)</h4>
      <p>Claude leads in bug complaints (5.5%) with reports centering on crashes and server errors. Google Gemini follows at 5.2%. Bug-themed reviews receive the highest engagement across the dataset (6.9 avg thumbs-up, up to 27.5 for Perplexity), meaning a single bug report can validate thousands of users' frustrations. Invest in mobile crash monitoring and reliability engineering to close the gap with Copilot (2.9%) and ChatGPT (2.1%).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rec-card" style="border-left: 4px solid #f59e0b;">
      <div class="rec-priority" style="color: #f59e0b;">P1 &mdash; High</div>
      <h4>3. Reduce Accuracy/Hallucination Complaints</h4>
      <p>Perplexity (6.4%) and ChatGPT (5.5%) lead in accuracy complaints, and these produce the harshest ratings (2.04 avg stars for Perplexity). Accuracy failures erode the core trust proposition of AI assistants. Invest in retrieval-augmented generation improvements, citation quality, and confidence calibration to differentiate on reliability. Claude's relatively lower accuracy complaint rate (4.3%) is a competitive advantage worth maintaining and messaging.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rec-card" style="border-left: 4px solid #f59e0b;">
      <div class="rec-priority" style="color: #f59e0b;">P1 &mdash; High</div>
      <h4>4. Mine the "Winnable Disappointed" Segment</h4>
      <p>11&ndash;13% of reviews across Claude, Perplexity, and Gemini show positive sentiment but low star ratings &mdash; users who see value but are blocked by specific issues. This is the highest-ROI retention segment: they've already expressed affinity. Build feedback loops (in-app surveys after low-star ratings, response-to-review programs) to identify and resolve their specific blockers.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rec-card" style="border-left: 4px solid #3b82f6;">
      <div class="rec-priority" style="color: #3b82f6;">P2 &mdash; Medium</div>
      <h4>5. Invest in Unicode-Robust Sentiment Analytics</h4>
      <p>Up to 14.6% of reviews (Google Gemini) produce zero-polarity VADER scores due to Unicode text, creating blind spots in sentiment analysis. Deploying a multilingual, Unicode-aware NLP model for internal analytics would improve competitive intelligence quality and avoid underestimating true negative sentiment in specific user populations.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rec-card" style="border-left: 4px solid #3b82f6;">
